      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "component_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "CVE-2026-118750 (GHSA-6527-9fp8-r4x6) is a denial of service in FileBufferingReadStream in the standalone ASP.NET Core 2.3 package Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities, versions 2.3.0 to 2.3.13, fixed in 2.3.14; the advisory lists no other ASP.NET Core version as affected (https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/512, https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6527-9fp8-r4x6). This owner does not contain a 2.3.x build of that assembly. Unpacked all 77 azure-functions-python packages published in the DHI Debian repository, 4.1053.100-1 to 4.1056.200-2, which are published for amd64 only, including the Azure Functions extension bundle each one carries. Each contains exactly one Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities.dll, in the Functions host directory (/usr/share/azure-functions-host), and in every package it is the ASP.NET Core 10 build: file versions 10.0.10 to 10.0.15 (assembly version 10.0.0.0) across the published packages. The extension bundle's dependency manifests (function.deps.json) name Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities 2.3.0 as a dependency, which is what scanners match, but the bundle ships no copy of that assembly, so no WebUtilities 2.3.x code is present in any published package."
